{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And I whirled them</b> — A difficult word in grammar, for it appears as though it belongs to the transitive verbs, and it would be correct to say ואסרם or ואסערם with a heavy [i.e., dagesh-bearing] root letter. And Rabbenu Marinus said: ואסער. And this is not correct, on account of \"upon all the nations.\" And the correct reading in my eyes: ואסער להם — \"and I whirled upon them with the storm of My spirit,\" and it is what scattered them upon all the nations." "<b>And he mentioned, \"and the land was desolate\"</b> — the opposite of \"and the Negev and the Shephelah shall be inhabited.\""], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "Resolved 'Rabbenu Marinus' as a proper name; the form ואסערם occurs once with dagesh-marking unclear in the manuscripts."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:18.295683217Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}